    {
      "id": "9smtInYCLCqBHLkMdHydL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3868.5658865216515,
      "y": -3522.0310155585316,
      "width": 495.3500061035156,
      "height": 609.5433134724492,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#20a048",
      "backgroundColor": "#181818",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "KiZnInf45DY03MmzX3woE",
      "index": "bU7zzzzzzzzzzzzvt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1490050226,
      "version": 2277,
      "versionNonce": 1569568578,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795461036428,
      "created": 1795437219563,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Back panel uses pause.pokemonDetail.background. \n{Name/Nickname}{Gender} and {Favorite Icon}{LockedIcon} go\nin the top color bar like the current name do in the current\npause menu. #ffffff color, font.silver\nOOR Level EXP bar: \n   - EXP top: #00baf3\n   - EXP bottom: #0d7f9d\n   - EXP empty top: #828282\n   - EXP empty bottom: #e7e7e7\n{Out of run Level} goes where the HP bar was. {TypeChip1}\n{TypeChip2} are right justified against the 45deg section. OOR\nlevel #ffffff, font.michroma\nLevel Up button uses neutral button. Single click gives EXP\nCandy until next full level. Shift-Click gives EXP to reach +10\nlevel. \"Give Until\" can be removed.\nStat Bars box uses the reference image where the numbers in\nfront of the bar are the base stat (Including per-pokemon\nupgrades). the bar is two pixels tall. the numbers on the right\nof the bar is the IV/EV value. the top bar is the IV value 0-31\nin color.stat*.light and the bottom bar is the EV value 0-252 in\ncolor.stat*.dark. Stat names use color.stat*.base. all text in\nfont.micrhoma \nThe toggle switches the Stat Bars section to our stat HEX\nusing the CRT off → on effect with the content of the box.\nthe box itself remains static.  \nNature #ffffff font.michroma\nAbility #ffffff font.michroma\nStarting Move box font.michroma colors as listed\n\nMoves button uses neutral button\nEXP Bag uses neutral button and opens EXP Bag Hover Pop-Up",
      "fontSize": 15.730150025095462,
      "baseFontSize": 15.730150025095462,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "kXjQzzqRSshzjYnP4LxOS",
      "originalText": "Back panel uses pause.pokemonDetail.background. \n{Name/Nickname}{Gender} and {Favorite Icon}{LockedIcon} go in the top color bar like the current name do in the current pause menu. #ffffff color, font.silver\nOOR Level EXP bar: \n   - EXP top: #00baf3\n   - EXP bottom: #0d7f9d\n   - EXP empty top: #828282\n   - EXP empty bottom: #e7e7e7\n{Out of run Level} goes where the HP bar was. {TypeChip1}{TypeChip2} are right justified against the 45deg section. OOR level #ffffff, font.michroma\nLevel Up button uses neutral button. Single click gives EXP Candy until next full level. Shift-Click gives EXP to reach +10 level. \"Give Until\" can be removed.\nStat Bars box uses the reference image where the numbers in front of the bar are the base stat (Including per-pokemon upgrades). the bar is two pixels tall. the numbers on the right of the bar is the IV/EV value. the top bar is the IV value 0-31 in color.stat*.light and the bottom bar is the EV value 0-252 in color.stat*.dark. Stat names use color.stat*.base. all text in font.micrhoma \nThe toggle switches the Stat Bars section to our stat HEX using the CRT off → on effect with the content of the box. the box itself remains static.  \nNature #ffffff font.michroma\nAbility #ffffff font.michroma\nStarting Move box font.michroma colors as listed\n\nMoves button uses neutral button\nEXP Bag uses neutral button and opens EXP Bag Hover Pop-Up",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
